    {
      "id": "pericles-prince-of-tyre/sceneI_27.4/p@27180",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CLEON.\nO Dionyza,\nWho wanteth food, and will not say he wants it,\nOr can conceal his hunger till he famish?\nOur tongues and sorrows do sound deep\nOur woes into the air; our eyes do weep,\nTill tongues fetch breath that may proclaim them louder;\nThat, if heaven slumber while their creatures want,\nThey may awake their helps to comfort them.\nI’ll then discourse our woes, felt several years,\nAnd wanting breath to speak, help me with tears.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
