    },
    {
      "id": "pericles-prince-of-tyre/sceneI_27.4/p@27761",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CLEON.\nThis Tarsus, o’er which I have the government,\nA city on whom plenty held full hand,\nFor riches strew’d herself even in the streets;\nWhose towers bore heads so high they kiss’d the clouds,\nAnd strangers ne’er beheld but wonder’d at;\nWhose men and dames so jetted and adorn’d,\nLike one another’s glass to trim them by:\nTheir tables were stored full to glad the sight,\nAnd not so much to feed on as delight;\nAll poverty was scorn’d, and pride so great,\nThe name of help grew odious to repeat.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "pericles-prince-of-tyre/sceneI_27.4/p@27761/line-1",
