      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CLEON.\nThe which when any shall not gratify,\nOr pay you with unthankfulness in thought,\nBe it our wives, our children, or ourselves,\nThe curse of heaven and men succeed their evils!\nTill when,—the which I hope shall ne’er be seen,—\nYour grace is welcome to our town and us.",
